2026-11-19 20:16:06 - Agent_20261119201419 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed the pydantic ReDoS group. Confirmed CVE-2024-3772-style ReDoS true positives in the "pretty email" regex in both the v2 and v1 code paths (package versions 2.3.0 / v1 1.10.12, both prior to the upstream fix): pydantic/networks.py:389-397 (_build_pretty_email_regex -> pretty_email_regex, used at line 413 on user-supplied EmailStr/validate_email input) and pydantic/v1/networks.py:704 (re.compile(r'([\\w ]*?) *<(.*)> *'), used at line 717). Dismissed the pydantic/json_schema.py:1827 nested-quantifier hit as a false positive: the regex is applied to internally generated core_ref metadata, not attacker input, and the quantifier nesting is over a disjoint character alphabet so it does not backtrack catastrophically. Query 3's string-literal results were the individual fragments of the same vulnerable networks.py regex, covered by the first finding.
